cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you refer to Brim, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Brim"
abstract: >-
  Brim is a free, open-source macOS menu bar app for Apple Silicon Macs. It runs
  several Claude Code accounts side by side (per-account usage, automatic
  account picking, moving a conversation to another account), ends leftover
  development processes when memory is tight, and bundles a system monitor,
  Port Manager, Kill Process, Cleaner, Uninstaller, Homebrew manager, app
  updates, clipboard history, keep awake and a Dynamic Island. It is a hard
  fork of Vorssaint.
authors:
  - given-names: "Eliseo"
    family-names: "Robles"
  - name: "Robles Consulting LLC"
repository-code: "https://github.com/eliseorobles/brim"
url: "https://eliseorobles.github.io/brim/"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
keywords:
  - macOS
  - menu bar app
  - Claude Code
  - multiple accounts
  - usage limits
  - system monitor
  - memory management
  - developer tools
  - Swift
  - SwiftUI
references:
